#   line 80: the source of the rule is in zone em1, and the MX names no zone: give the networks behind em1 with --zone-network; port 0, which the MX does not take
#   line 79: the source of the rule is in zone em1, and the MX names no zone: give the networks behind em1 with --zone-network
#   line 78: the source of the rule is in zone em1, and the MX names no zone: give the networks behind em1 with --zone-network; port 0, which the MX does not take
#   line 69: the source of the rule is in zone em1, and the MX names no zone: give the networks behind em1 with --zone-network
#   line 69.2: the source of the rule is in zone em1, and the MX names no zone: give the networks behind em1 with --zone-network
#   line 66: the source of the rule is in zone em1, and the MX names no zone: give the networks behind em1 with --zone-network; an ICMP type, or a protocol other than TCP, UDP, ICMP and ICMPv6: the MX has no field for it
#   line 65: the source of the rule is in zone em1, em2, and the MX names no zone: give the networks behind em1, em2 with --zone-network; an ICMP type, or a protocol other than TCP, UDP, ICMP and ICMPv6: the MX has no field for it
